@aoyako Thanks a lot for the feedback! @malfet I just wanted to follow up and kindly ask the developers to take another look at this issue when time permits. It seems that others have successfully reproduced the problem, which helps confirm it’s not an isolated case. Really appreciate the help and verification from the community!

Let me know if any additional logs or simplified repros would help—I’d be happy to assist.

Thanks again!

> [@williamwen42](https://github.com/williamwen42) can you check if setting `torch._dynamo.config.wrap_top_frame = True` fixes the `conv.compile()` case? If so it might be related to [#158455](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/158455).

@StrongerXi I encountered the same issue when using PyTorch 2.5.1, but there seems to be no `wrap_top_frame` in `torch._dynamo.config`. 

Could you please advise on how to resolve this?
